# History: rcan-assurance. RCAN's canonical JSON section says that names sort in "Unicode
# code-point order" and, in the same section, that the scheme "matches RFC 8785", which sorts by
# UTF-16 code units. No published test vector told the two apart, and the two SDKs disagreed
# past the published vectors.
#
# Written as Tilth, the section binds two edges to one operation. The checker compares their
# conformance packs and reports each input where they disagree (T026), with no oracle and no
# implementation: one input where the key orders differ, and two lone-surrogate inputs that
# RFC 8785, read strictly, refuses.
tilth 0.1

spec rcan-canonical 3.2

op canonical
  input value any

edge json/sorted-codepoint via canonical value
edge json/rfc8785 via canonical value
